== Effects ==
* Isaac's tears travel a short distance, then reverse direction and return to Isaac.
** The tears are constantly pulled towards Isaac; if Isaac moves after shooting, the tears will always return to him.
** {{dlc|r}} The distance the tears travel before rebounding is determined by Isaac's Range stat.
* {{dlc|nr}} +1.5 [[range]].
* {{dlc|nr}} +1 [[tear falling speed]].
* {{dlc|r}} 2x + 1.5 [[range]], +1.5 [[damage]], -1 [[luck]].
* 1.6x [[shot speed]] multiplier.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|Anti-Gravity}}: The tears will slowly move towards Isaac instead of remaining stationary. Releasing the fire button will launch the tears as usual.
* {{dlc|na}} {{i|Brimstone}}: Overrides My Reflection.
** {{dlc|anr}} Makes the beam curve when moving. It has the same effect on Azazel's mini-brimstone and doubles the range.
** {{dlc|r}} The laser makes a thin loop in front of Isaac, and fires the normal laser backwards.
* {{i|Continuum}}: If tears cross the border of the room, they will move towards Isaac from their new position rather than crossing back across the border.
* {{i|Compound Fracture}} / {{i|The Parasite}}/{{i|Cricket's Body}}: Split tears will move towards Isaac.
* {{i|Dr. Fetus}}: '''Not recommended.''' The bombs will slide back towards Isaac after having reached a certain distance.
** When combined with {{i|Rocket in a Jar}}, the rockets will not explode unless they hit an obstacle or enemy, making this much safer.
* {{i|Epic Fetus}}: Overrides My Reflection.
* {{i|Euthanasia}}: Needles from Euthanasia bursts will move towards Isaac.
* {{i|Flat Stone}}: Tears bounce away from and then back towards Isaac. However, unless you have range ups, this generally results in tears slowing down then dissipating rather than actually returning.
* {{i|Haemolacria}}: Range becomes extremely high, making Haemolacria tears follow Isaac for a long time before hitting the ground. Burst tears do not have a boomerang effect.
* {{i|Ipecac}}: '''Not recommended.''' The explosive tears will begin flying back towards Isaac after having reached a certain distance.
* {{i|Lachryphagy}}: Tears will move towards Isaac and can still be fed and burst. The bursted tears will also move towards Isaac.
* {{i|A Lump of Coal}}: The tears increase in damage as they are pulled towards Isaac.
* {{i|The Ludovico Technique}}: The tear will slowly move towards Isaac, and the shot speed increase allows the tear to be moved much faster.
* {{Dlc|anr}}{{i|Mom's Knife}}: No effect, as the knife already has this effect.
** {{Dlc|r}}The stat changes carry over, but the knife's trajectory does not.
* {{i|Montezuma's Revenge}}: Causes the beam range behind Isaac to become significantly increased as well as having a short range similar to Azazel's beam in front of him. This greatly eases the use of this item allowing for high DPS.
* {{dlc|nr}}{{i|My Reflection}}: No further stat changes.
** {{dlc|r}} Damage and luck changes stack, range and shot speed don't.
* [[Piercing tears]]: Despite the piercing effect, tears cannot damage the same enemy multiple times.
* {{i|Pop!}}: Tears constantly swarm around Isaac, quickly filling the room.
* {{i|Proptosis}}: At base tear size, tears disappear before they can return to Isaac.
* {{i|Pupula Duplex|r}}: Tears will spin like boomerangs, the effect is purely cosmetic.
* {{i|Revelation}}: The laser makes a thin loop in front of Isaac, and fires the normal laser backwards.
* {{i|Rubber Cement}}: Isaac's tears will continually be pulled towards him, effectively reducing the chances that tears will bounce.
* {{i|Spoon Bender}}: If tears are close enough to an enemy, it will home in and damage them. If not, they will return to Isaac.
* {{dlc|r}}{{i|Stop Watch}}: Slightly reduces the distance tears travel before returning to Isaac, while slightly increasing the distance tears travel while returning to Isaac.
* {{i|Strange Attractor}}: '''Not recommended.''' While it may make it easier to hit enemies, it also makes it much easier for them to be attracted to Isaac, surrounding him.
* {{dlc|na}}{{i|Technology}}: Overrides My Reflection.
** {{dlc|anr}}Makes the beam curve when moving.
** {{dlc|r}} The laser makes a thin loop in front of Isaac, and fires the normal laser backwards.
* {{dlc|na}}{{i|Technology 2}} / {{i|Tech.5}}
** {{dlc|anr}}Tears return to character and the beams curve when moving.
** {{dlc|r}} The laser makes a thin loop in front of Isaac, and fires the normal laser backwards.
* {{i|Tech X}}: Stat effects of My Reflection remain but the boomerang effect does not.
* {{i|Tiny Planet}}: The orbital tears will move faster to stay in orbit around Isaac, making aiming easier.
** {{dlc|r}} Increases the radius of the orbital tears.
* {{i|Trisagion|a+nr}}: Makes the beams much longer as they move away from and then back towards Isaac.
** {{dlc|r}} The beams are in the form of a thin loop which cover a larger area, and the beams return to Isaac.
* {{t|Whip Worm}}: Further increases shot speed, making Isaac's tears travel much farther forward before returning to Isaac.
** {{dlc|r}} Shots travel the same distance forward, but loop back further before hitting the ground.

